After a bit of frustration, I've gotten 3.1 running. _Very_ nice. I've 
noticed some interesting new things going on with the characters...

Alignment is no longer fixed for each class. I decided to try a priest, and 
was _very_ surprised to find that goblins were friendly to me. Yes, priests 
can be of any alignment now. I've seen neutral valkyries as well, and there 
are certainly many other possibilities.

Knights start with intrinsic _jumping_ of all things.

Archaeologists (my favorite class) start with _terrible_ armor. No leather 
armor for them -- its a leather jacket now, worth only one point of AC. And 
the fedora is worthless. No AC value at all.

Priests can start with wolfsbane as well as garlic.

Has anyone else noticed new and exciting things going on at the start?

To sleep or not to sleep, that is the question...happy hacking!
